WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:03.020
Did Qatar "buy" fans?

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.460
Did Russia threaten to "ban" the World Cup
in Qatar?

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.270
And will a match at this World Cup not last
90 minutes but 100?

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:17.010
All these rumors are actually circulating
on the net about the FIFA World Cup in Qatar.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.130
And even more.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.740
But not everything is actually true.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:21.990
We have checked that for you.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.340
But first, a few facts about the biggest sporting
event of the year:

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.630
This is the first ever World Cup to be held
in the Middle East.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.100
It is the first World Cup to be held in winter.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.309
Qatar is the smallest host country in World
Cup history.

00:00:36.309 --> 00:00:40.739
The World Cup in Qatar is by far the most
expensive tournament ever.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.010
But will the tournament be played all the
way to the final?

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.989
Social media users sowed doubt about that:

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:51.920
after Russia was banned by FIFA for attacking
Ukraine, President Vladimir Putin reportedly

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.989
threatened, "Russia will play at the Qatar
2022 FIFA world cup or there will be no world

00:00:57.989 --> 00:00:59.550
cup to talk about."

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.760
As this this viral Facebook post suggests.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.760
False

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.909
There is no proof that Putin said that and
no media has reported about it.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:15.119
Even on the Kremlin website, where all Putin's
speeches are documented, there is no mention

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:16.119
of it.

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:21.750
Fact is that only FIFA can cancel or stop
the World Cup, not Russia.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.530
This poster also caused uproar.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.420
It was shared on the web in dozens of languages.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.149
It allegedly shows rules for the World Cup,
such as that alcohol and homosexuality are

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:35.409
forbidden in Qatar.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:36.970
Misleading

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:42.200
Contrary to what many people thought, the
poster does not come from the Qatari government.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.420
The Qatari citizens' initiative "Reflect Your
Respect," which has been calling on foreigners

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:54.880
in particular to respect Qatari customs since
2014, is apparently responsible for the poster.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.039
And what about the content of the poster?

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:03.149
The Supreme Committee responsible for the
World Cup said it showed "factually incorrect

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:04.149
information."

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:06.329
So, which of the bans are true?

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:08.220
Let's take a closer look.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:14.260
With regard to alcohol consumption, the law
in Qatar is clear: Alcohol is not prohibited,

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.740
but drinking it in public is.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.209
This is punishable by up to six months in
prison.

00:02:20.209 --> 00:02:24.440
Dating, however, is not forbidden under Qatari
law.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.150
And homosexuality?

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.270
That is a punishable offense in Qatar.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:34.420
Qatari law punishes it with one to five years
in prison.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.420
Homosexuality and the World Cup in Qatar - a
topic that provides for discussions as seen

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.640
after a recent statement by the Qatari World
Cup ambassador.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:49.580
And the debate of homosexuality and the World
Cup in Qatar lead to fakes like this one:

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:54.879
Here Cristiano Ronaldo and Lionel Messi are
allegedly kissing.

00:02:54.879 --> 00:03:00.250
And Qatar is calling for the two to be banned
from the World Cup, according to this Facebook

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.190
post, which has been shared thousands of times.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.390
Both are fake, of course.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:12.000
It is a photomontage, meant as satire, with
which a youth format on Swiss television in

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.220
2021 wanted to draw attention to the treatment
of homosexuality in football.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:23.750
And Qatar's demand that Messi and Ronaldo
be excluded from the World Cup is completely

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.750
made up.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:30.560
The same goes for this story: FIFA is said
to have excluded Algeria's fans from the World

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.370
Cup, as is claimed on Facebook and Youtube.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.689
They are not allowed to travel to Qatar.

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:39.870
False

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.610
Algeria did not qualify for the World Cup.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.299
However, fans from Algeria were not excluded.

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:52.790
We could not find any such rules or entry
requirements, neither from FIFA nor from Qatar.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.050
Speaking of fans.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:04:00.579
This news made international headlines: Qatar
is said to have "bought" fans.

00:04:00.579 --> 00:04:03.260
That's right, at least in part.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:10.120
Qatar has invited selected international football
fans and paid for their flights, hotels, accommodation

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.500
and even given some pocket money.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.919
The Dutch broadcaster NOS was the first to
report on it.

00:04:16.919 --> 00:04:20.090
And we have spoken with fans who received
this offer.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:29.930
SOT Joseph Delage, Fan aus Frankreich: "The
offer included the air ticket, the hotel costs

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:35.350
and a ticket for the opening match.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:39.699
But you had to stay for the entire first round.

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:44.330
The idea was also that you can participate
in cultural and sports activities."

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:49.419
"Plus: We are given a per diem for meals.

00:04:49.419 --> 00:04:53.780
After that we are on our own to buy our match
tickets.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:58.229
We are on our own to enjoy the tournament
as it is.

00:04:58.229 --> 00:05:00.770
That’s everything in a nutshell."

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:07.250
The Supreme Committee responsible for the
World Cup confirmed to us on request: flights,

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:11.820
hotels and accommodation costs are paid for
selected fans.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:16.699
Nevertheless, they were not "bought", according
to Qatar.

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:24.350
Because no consideration in the sense of "promotion"
was expected, reports about it are "absolutely

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.020
false."

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.690
But is that true?

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:33.250
In our research, we come across an official
paper that speaks a different language.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:40.350
In the "code of conduct," Qatar expects participating
fans to do exactly that: promote.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:45.861
Fans are supposed to agree to support the
Qatar World Cup "by liking and sharing" social

00:05:45.861 --> 00:05:54.560
media posts, using the hashtag #IAMAFAN and
tagging the official Roadto2022 channel.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:06:00.320
Qatar also advises participating fans that
their posts will be "monitored."

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:05.050
Qatar could require fans to delete posts that
violate the Code of Conduct.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:10.620
And "disparaging the World Cup OR Qatar" is
not appropriate.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.789
According to our information, the Code of
Conduct was not presented to all fans.

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:21.300
But for the fans who were sent the document,
it's fair to say that Qatar indirectly paid

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:29.480
them with flights, hotels, tickets, and pocket
money - in exchange for social media reach.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:35.710
And in this case, Qatar is said to have paid
fans as well, as social media users claim.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:42.650
During fan marches in Qatar, thousands walked
through Doha wearing jerseys of the participating

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.020
nations.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:56.910
According to our information, most of them
are migrant workers, many from India.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:09.560
Qatar has offered them heavily discounted
tickets to World Cup matches.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:14.410
And it is not the first time that Qatar has
been accused of employing migrant workers

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.960
as sport fans.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.840
Qatar is also fighting back against these
headlines: International media accuse the

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.130
kingdom of restricting press freedom.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:29.530
This is because camera teams have to sign
a list of conditions and bans that massively

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.389
restrict their work.

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:37.210
Qatar's Supreme Committee contradicts via
Twitter: Filming is allowed after obtaining

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.860
permits.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:45.110
And journalists can "report freely and without
interference" in Qatar.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.110
False

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:51.300
According to our research, truly free reporting
from Qatar without state interference is not

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.300
possible.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:58.050
Government buildings, religious institutions,
universities, hospitals, homes and private

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:02.120
businesses may not be filmed without permission.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:06.360
This is also confirmed by the International
Federation of Journalists (IFJ).

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:11.639
These restrictions would prevent the media
from reporting on topics of public interest,

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:13.949
such as human rights violations.

00:08:13.949 --> 00:08:20.449
We know that Doha News has been suspended
for a long time as well for their reporting.

00:08:20.449 --> 00:08:33.800
We know that The New York Times was not able
to make its stories available on certain specific

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:37.599
issues, such as LGBTQIA+.

00:08:37.599 --> 00:08:47.260
"Secondly, we are also concerned about a law
that exists in Qatar which makes any spreading

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:55.300
of fake news or rumors subject to very heavy
fines and up to five, five years jail term."

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.890
Particularly interesting: Qatar's government
controls who reports when and how about the

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.899
guest workers in the country - their poor
working conditions have been a controversial

00:09:05.899 --> 00:09:44.640
topic for years.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:50.130
Journalists are therefore hindered and censored
in their work in Qatar - a circumstance that

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:53.050
many observe with great concern.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:56.380
But there are some bizarre rumors about the
upcoming FIFA World Cup.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.990
Like this fake that made us laugh.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:04.430
Here, a Facebook user claims that during this
tournament of the World Cup a match would

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.590
last 100 minutes instead of 90.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:08.630
Really?!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.760
Of course, this is false.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:17.070
A football match lasts 90 minutes, and that's
how it will stay in this World Cup as well.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:22.680
And FIFA has also confirmed: there will be
no changes in the match length.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.320
Some things will be different during this
World Cup.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.060
But some things will remain the same.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.570
Have you come across more World Cup fakes?

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:36.180
Then write to us: in the comment section below
or to factchecking@dw.com

